1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,040
 (dramatic music)

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:03,680
 - Previously on Elephant Diaries,

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,840
 I met up with an old friend, Wendy.

4
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,680
 She seems to be having a bit of an identity crisis,

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:12,000
 more interested in interacting with people than elephants.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,520
 - And a tiny three-week-old baby elephant

7
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,980
 was rescued when he collapsed in the wild.

8
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:21,880
 After a few days in the orphanage in Nairobi,

9
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,520
 Daphne made a devastating discovery.

10
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:28,440
 - Unfortunately, one eye is blind.

11
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,520
 The other one looks like it's getting blind.

12
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:36,200
 Say we've got a blind elephant.

13
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,160
 (dramatic music)

14
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:57,680
 - We're following the stories of a group

15
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:00,240
 of orphaned baby elephants in Kenya.

16
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,880
 All of them have been rescued by

17
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,120
 the David Sheldrick Wildlife Trust

18
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:07,360
 and brought to a unique orphanage in Nairobi.

19
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,960
 Here, they're reared and nurtured

20
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,880
 by a team of 20 dedicated keepers

21
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,400
 under the guidance of the orphanage founder,

22
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,960
 Dane Daphne Sheldrick.

23
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:20,320
 The ultimate aim is to get them back to the wild

24
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:22,160
 in Savo National Park.

25
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:29,040
 - Undololo is the newest arrival,

26
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:32,920
 and despite his blindness, he's making steady progress.

27
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,160
 The other orphans are out in the bush,

28
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:38,760
 but for now, Undololo is being kept in isolation.

29
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:42,840
 Everyone adores him, especially head keeper Edwin.

30
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:47,840
 - It's a very clever boy, a very selective

31
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:51,920
 because at the moment he tries to smell around

32
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:56,600
 all the hippas and can find out the feveris among the hippas.

33
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:59,560
 And in return, they attend to his every need,

34
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,040
 protecting his delicate ears with sun cream

35
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,480
 and shading him from the midday sun.

36
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:07,920
 They're determined to give him the best chance of survival.

37
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,040
 And what's giving everyone hope is that

38
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:12,840
 the vet thinks his blindness might be curable.

39
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:16,480
 - It's everybody is pity about him

40
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,520
 and everybody is worried about him.

41
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:20,920
 So everybody wants to take care of him.

42
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:23,680
 Everybody wants to be concerned with him.

43
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:28,680
 Everyone wants to be close to him to see that he can actually improve.

44
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,880
 - Only time will tell if his eyesight will get better,

45
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,560
 but hopefully he should be well enough

46
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:36,320
 to meet the other little orphans very soon.

47
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,520
 But for now, playing with the big boys and girls

48
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,280
 is out of the question.

49
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,560
 Their games are far too exciting,

50
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,560
 and there's a reason for this.

51
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:47,680
 - All of these elephants have had a really tough start to life.

52
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,680
 They've all experienced tragedy,

53
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:52,920
 and they've all had to grow up and learn lessons far quicker

54
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,760
 than they would have done in the wild.

55
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:57,200
 But nevertheless, they're still very young,

56
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,800
 so it's still important for them to get some exercise,

57
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,920
 let off some steam and have some fun.

58
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:05,560
 And what better way to do that than a good old game of football?

59
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,140
 (upbeat music)

60
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:12,520
 - These games are more than just a chance

61
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:15,440
 for the orphans to run rings around the keepers.

62
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,600
 Playing is a great way for this little herd

63
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,800
 of unrelated babies to bond with each other.

64
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:25,500
 (upbeat music)

65
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:55,920
 (crowd chattering)

66
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,500
 (upbeat music)

67
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:01,500
 (crowd chattering)

68
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:04,080
 (upbeat music)

69
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:07,080
 (upbeat music)

70
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,000
 - The friendships the little elephants form

71
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,440
 here in Nairobi are for life.

72
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:13,160
 Because when you've lost your family,

73
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,400
 friends are all you've got.

74
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:17,640
 And these bonds will stay with the orphans

75
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:20,120
 as they reach the age to leave the nursery

76
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:22,400
 and go through to the next stage in their journey

77
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,660
 back to the wild.

78
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:28,480
 - And this second stage is the one I'm following

79
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,280
 down here in Sarvo National Park.

80
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:33,920
 I'm on my way to one of the trust two release sites

81
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:36,880
 to catch up with an orphan called Wendy.

82
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,440
 - This is a thumber and it has to be one

83
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,640
 of the wildest places in Kenya.

84
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:42,360
 But it's also where the little elephants

85
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,880
 from Nairobi or furniture brought

86
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:47,960
 to begin the process of introducing them back into the wild.

87
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:51,160
 But not only is it wild, it is stunningly beautiful

88
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,360
 and a safe haven for the elephants too.

89
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,200
 Perfect.

90
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:58,120
 - Down here, the elephants spend the night

91
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:02,040
 in open-air stockades and go out into the bush each day

92
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,120
 to learn everything they need to know

93
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,700
 about life in the wild.

94
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:10,320
 But my main concern here at the moment

95
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:12,800
 is to see how Wendy is getting on.

96
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,320
 At the age of four, she should be settled

97
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,840
 into life with her elephant family

98
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:21,600
 and forming close bonds with other females in her herd.

99
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,800
 But because she was raised by humans

100
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:27,200
 from the day she was born, Wendy has other ideas.

101
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:30,800
 - You can see how Wendy, really at the moment,

102
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,560
 is much more interested in people

103
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:33,920
 than she is in the other elephants.

104
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:36,040
 I mean, she's completely isolated here.

105
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,240
 That's not what we want.

106
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:39,200
 We want her to be an elephant.

107
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:41,840
 But at the same time, we are her family.

108
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,040
 The keepers are her family.

109
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:46,840
 We have to play that role for her if it's what she needs.

110
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:50,280
 And each of these animals are very distinct characters.

111
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:54,160
 Right now, Wendy seems almost lonely at times

112
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,920
 as if she doesn't quite know what to do with herself.

113
00:05:56,920 --> 00:06:00,720
 - This is a complex problem

114
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:04,200
 and shows how sensitive and intelligent elephants are.

115
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,320
 But Daphne and the keepers are hoping

116
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,600
 that they have come up with a solution.

117
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:11,000
 Crucially, it's something which will help her bond

118
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,360
 with other elephants.

119
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:16,520
 And it involves some of the little orphans up in Nairobi

120
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,400
 with Michaela.

121
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:21,120
 - There are 10 of them living here at the moment,

122
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:23,840
 but things are about to change.

123
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:26,400
 - The nursery is a great place for all these orphans

124
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,640
 to start their journey back into the wild.

125
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:31,240
 However, they all get to an age around the age of two

126
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:33,640
 where they need to move on to the next stage

127
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,200
 of their rehabilitation.

128
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,520
 Now, currently in this group,

129
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,840
 there are three elephants that are big enough

130
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,440
 to make that move.

131
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,840
 - So how is this going to help Wendy?

132
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:46,080
 When she was in Nairobi, she was the mini matriarch.

133
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:49,120
 And this is the key to the whole plan.

134
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,000
 - What they're going to do is when they move

135
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
 the new group of little elephants

136
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,760
 from the orphanage in Nairobi up here to Ethumba,

137
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:59,040
 they're going to separate them in one part of the stockade

138
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,120
 and they're going to put Wendy with them.

139
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,920
 Now that'll suddenly give her a role again.

140
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,720
 It'll give her a purpose in life.

141
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:07,160
 It'll make her a mini matriarch again.

142
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,720
 I just hope the plan works.

143
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:16,280
 Here in Nairobi, preparations are in full swing

144
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:20,320
 for this move, which is due to happen early tomorrow morning.

145
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:23,480
 So for the keepers, it's time to say goodbye

146
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,080
 to the three who are leaving.

147
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:29,360
 Among them is a little elephant called a rock.

148
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:32,960
 He's the smallest and the most nervous of the three.

149
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:35,840
 The move could be pretty stressful for him,

150
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,800
 but he's really going to need a big friend

151
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:39,660
 like Wendy to take care of him.

152
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:43,960
 So it's as important for a rock as it is for Wendy

153
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,520
 that the plan works.

154
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:53,240
 Back at the stables, the trucks are ready

155
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:56,320
 and waiting to take all three to their new life.

156
00:07:56,320 --> 00:08:06,720
 After an early start, the three little lilies from Nairobi

157
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:09,080
 are well on their way down to join Wendy

158
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,840
 and the others here in Ephumba.

159
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:15,760
 It's eight hot hours in a truck

160
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,400
 driving deep into Sarvo National Park,

161
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:21,040
 which will be home for the rest of their lives.

162
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:27,600
 Here they come.

163
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:33,560
 They seem none the worse for their ordeal.

164
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:37,840
 Although I have to say, little a rock does look quite anxious.

165
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,880
 There must be tough for them, different voices,

166
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,600
 different sounds, different smells,

167
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,120
 a whole different place for them.

168
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:48,640
 But the one thing they've got, of course, is the keepers.

169
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:51,400
 The keepers are the continuity in this whole project.

170
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:54,040
 And wherever they are, Nairobi, Ephumba,

171
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,880
 they will be very much loved.

172
00:08:55,880 --> 00:09:02,280
 This one, the littlest one, a rock, you can tell.

173
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:05,240
 It's whole body language says, "I'm nervous.

174
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,320
 "I'm not sure where I am."

175
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,280
 In eight hours you've moved me,

176
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,800
 you've changed my whole world.

177
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:15,360
 Paul Littler rock, I mean, he looks so scared.

178
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:17,480
 He really does need a bigger elephant

179
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,360
 to take him under her wing,

180
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:22,120
 and we're all hoping it's going to be Wendy.

181
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,480
 Okay, here come the other elephants,

182
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,960
 and amongst them is Wendy.

183
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,120
 This could be crucial.

184
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:29,680
 (screaming)

185
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:40,320
 Okay, what is that saying, elephant?

186
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,320
 (screaming)

187
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:43,320
 I reckon it says there's something going on here

188
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:45,320
 and we want to know what it is.

189
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:50,320
 The whole herd are so excited,

190
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,320
 and the little ones are being thoroughly checked over.

191
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:57,320
 Just reassuring, just touching, feeling.

192
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,320
 Are you okay?

193
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:59,320
 Everything's fine, don't worry.

194
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:02,320
 You're in a new place, but it's going to be okay.

195
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:06,320
 A rock needs some reassurance, so where is Wendy?

196
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:10,320
 There she is, and how typical she's taking no interest,

197
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,320
 just doing her own thing.

198
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:17,320
 Let's hope the enthusiasm of the others rubs off on her,

199
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:20,320
 and she starts to feel maternal towards these little ones.

200
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:23,320
 She's going to be put in charge of them in a stock A tonight,

201
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:27,320
 and during the night is when a rock will need her most.

202
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:34,320
 But it's not only the A Thumba herd meeting new friends.

203
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:37,320
 Up in Nairobi, the keepers have decided

204
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:41,320
 that Underlolo is finally ready to meet the other orphans.

205
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:44,320
 He's been kept apart from them till now,

206
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:46,320
 as he's been too weak to meet them.

207
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:49,320
 But now he's getting so much stronger,

208
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:51,320
 it's time to say hello.

209
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:58,320
 Despite their overwhelming curiosity,

210
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:01,320
 the bigger orphans are being very gentle and careful,

211
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:05,320
 and seem to be able to sense Underlolo's fragility.

212
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:10,320
 But doting Edwin and the keepers are watching very closely

213
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,320
 to make sure their precious little elephant is coping.

214
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:27,320
 The meeting has gone well,

215
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:30,320
 but it'll be a long time before Underlolo is ready

216
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:34,320
 to join the whole gang for their daily walks out into the bush.

217
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:37,320
 And the little elephant is led back to his stable

218
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:40,320
 for a much-needed rest.

219
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:49,320
 Down here in A Thumba, the L is ahead for bed.

220
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:52,320
 An area of the Stockade has been sectioned off

221
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:56,320
 so that Wendy can be put in charge of the three new arrivals.

222
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:59,320
 This is her chance to be a mini matriarch again,

223
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:03,320
 and for O'Rock, a chance to get some much-needed TLC.

224
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:07,320
 It's a little bit like kids at their first night at boarding school.

225
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:10,320
 The three new ones, off by themselves,

226
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:12,320
 where they feel safest with the keepers.

227
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:14,320
 The three that know the ropes, including Wendy,

228
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,320
 are just very relaxed.

229
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:17,320
 As you'd expect, they know the routine here.

230
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,320
 Our new ones don't yet.

231
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:24,320
 Little O'Rock seems quite stressed and is looking for comfort,

232
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,320
 but no one is interested.

233
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:32,320
 You can imagine how different though this is.

234
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,320
 This set up for our three little elephants from Nairobi,

235
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:37,320
 because normally, at this time of the day in the evening,

236
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:39,320
 they'd be going back to a stable.

237
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:42,320
 Their own place to sleep with their keeper.

238
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,320
 Suddenly, this is big and scary.

239
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:46,320
 What's this about?

240
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:50,320
 Poor little O'Rock is getting pushed around

241
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,320
 and it's windy that's doing it.

242
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:55,320
 There are a couple of other older elephants in there as well,

243
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:57,320
 and they're following her lead, pushing and shoving.

244
00:12:57,320 --> 00:13:00,320
 This is not quite going to plan.

245
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:04,320
 But what they don't realise is they're being watched from next door.

246
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:08,320
 You see the way Nastalock, she's one of the bigger elephants,

247
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:12,320
 is just thinking what's happening here.

248
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:16,320
 I want to go and check those little ones out.

249
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:19,320
 And that's exactly what you'd expect for one of these bigger elephants.

250
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,320
 Acting as an auntie.

251
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:26,320
 She's not the matriarch, but she's a very, very caring elephant.

252
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:30,320
 She's desperate to get in there and look after the little ones,

253
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:32,320
 but this is supposed to be Wendy's job.

254
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:35,320
 You know, Wendy is so naughty.

255
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,320
 It's not what I expected.

256
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:39,320
 I was hoping that she was going to sort of smother these little ones

257
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:42,320
 with a bit of love, but instead it's just like, you know,

258
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,320
 "What are you doing here?"

259
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:45,320
 And she's pushing them out of the way.

260
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,320
 You can see right there.

261
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:50,320
 Actually getting quite shabby, quite bushy.

262
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:53,320
 Hang on, what's this?

263
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:56,320
 Okay, the keepers are putting Nastalot in with the little ones,

264
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:59,320
 and they certainly look pleased to see, you know.

265
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:02,320
 Oh, look. Just look at them.

266
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:05,320
 Now that's interesting.

267
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:09,320
 That was Wendy just being basically told, sorry.

268
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:12,320
 You're not going to stay with those little ones.

269
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:14,320
 Maybe she was being a bit too rough.

270
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:21,320
 Nastalot's immediately taking over the babysitting of these little ones,

271
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,320
 comforting and soothing them.

272
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,320
 You can see the effect she's having.

273
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:29,320
 They're so much more relaxed, and the whole atmosphere is calm right down.

274
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:34,320
 So for the first night, these little ones are going to have a very,

275
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:36,320
 very big sister, and it's not going to be Wendy.

276
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:43,320
 But the big question is, what's going to happen to Wendy?

277
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:47,320
 How are they ever going to get her to bond with the rest of the herd now?

278
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:58,320
 It's been a few weeks since the little blind calf,

279
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:02,320
 and Delono arrived in a terrible state at the Nairobi nursery,

280
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:05,320
 and he's making really good progress.

281
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:09,320
 He goes on daily outings, and the keepers have come up with a simple,

282
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:12,320
 but effective way to help him cope.

283
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:23,320
 The first day we took him out, he was very happy to go out with the keeper,

284
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:26,320
 trying to make a sound with the stick,

285
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:30,320
 and he actually was following the sound and the keepers well.

286
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:34,320
 He knew that because he could not see, could not use his eyes,

287
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:38,320
 but he could use that to direct him to show where the keepers are,

288
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:41,320
 and he was very happy to spend out the day with the keepers well.

289
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:46,320
 He's got a strong spirit to live.

290
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,320
 He actually has the desire to go on,

291
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,320
 despite the fact that he can't see.

292
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:53,320
 You see, he wants to run around with the bush,

293
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:57,320
 and sometimes he's the tree, so he doesn't mind being blind.

294
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:01,320
 He wants to behave like a real, wide elephant.

295
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,320
 Despite the fact he's blind.

296
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:07,320
 He's still under treatment for his eye condition,

297
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:10,320
 but it's too early to tell if it's working.

298
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:15,320
 Unfortunately, he's not yet ready to go out with the rest of the orphans.

299
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:20,320
 He could never keep up, let alone cope with the rough and tumble of their daily outings.

300
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:23,320
 In the afternoons, it's often time for a bit of exploration,

301
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:26,320
 and today we're taking our little orphans to the quarry.

302
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:32,320
 The quarry is full of beautiful, soft, iron-rich red earth,

303
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,320
 and the Emmys love it.

304
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:38,320
 Every time these elephants come to this quarry, they seem to have a good time.

305
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:42,320
 They just love to get stuck in and have a good old dust bar.

306
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:44,320
 It does have a purpose.

307
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:47,320
 It cleans them, it protects them from the sun, gets rid of parasites.

308
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:48,320
 But you know what?

309
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:53,320
 At this age, I think it's more to do with having fun and just getting dirty.

310
00:16:53,320 --> 00:17:06,320
 This is actually very funny this bit here.

311
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:09,320
 They seem to be using it as a slide.

312
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:14,320
 And once one elephant does it, another comes along and has a go.

313
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:18,320
 But McKenna, the smallest elephant here,

314
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:22,320
 is only interested in playing with the herd's mini-matriarch, Luolene.

315
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:26,320
 These two have a very close and loving bond.

316
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:30,320
 And it's one of the wonderful things about elephants,

317
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:34,320
 the way they form these deep, lifelong friendships with each other.

318
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:40,320
 This is something I'm hoping to see,

319
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:43,320
 as I head back towards the A-thumba Stockade.

320
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:46,320
 It's been a couple of weeks since I was last here,

321
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:50,320
 and I'm hoping that Wendy has started to bond again with the other elephants.

322
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:53,320
 But first, I want to check out Iraq.

323
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:58,320
 As the keepers say, he's formed a strong attachment to one of the older elephants,

324
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,320
 and I've arrived just in time for midday milk.

325
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:04,320
 Look at that, look at the dust, look at the excitement.

326
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:08,320
 This is the last group of elephants, and amongst them there, in the middle.

327
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:11,320
 That's the one I've been waiting for, that's Iraq.

328
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:15,320
 Now, here's one of the ones that we moved from Nairobi just recently.

329
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:20,320
 And he has made a relationship with Nacilok, she's like his mum.

330
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:24,320
 And wherever she goes, he tries to follow, just coming through the middle here.

331
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:31,320
 The tiniest of all, looking just a touch confused, but knows what's good for him.

332
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:39,320
 And just going past him, I think that's Nacilok.

333
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:41,320
 That's his surrogate mother.

334
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:44,320
 Just a touch of nervousness, and you'd expect it.

335
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:50,320
 This little elephant didn't come to the orphanage until he was 18 months old.

336
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:53,320
 So he knew all about his wild family.

337
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:55,320
 He knew what he was missing.

338
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:58,320
 When he was orphaned, his mother got sick, she died.

339
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:03,320
 And a year and a half, he was suddenly torn away from his complete support system.

340
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,320
 Look.

341
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:09,320
 Now, you see, nervous, where's mum?

342
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:11,320
 Where's my new mum?

343
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:13,320
 He's looking for Nacilok.

344
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,320
 Where is she?

345
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,320
 He's on the search, look.

346
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:19,320
 Look at the difference between him and the other elephants.

347
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:22,320
 All the other elephants, quiet, relaxed.

348
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,320
 And he's looking for somebody.

349
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,320
 Here comes Nacilok.

350
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:29,320
 See the trunk go out.

351
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,320
 And that's what he needs right now.

352
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:39,320
 He needs that reassurance to keep us and not enough for him.

353
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:44,320
 And that's the reason why Nacilok actually joins a rock.

354
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:48,320
 To keep him calm, to keep him settled.

355
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,320
 Totally different behavior now.

356
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:54,320
 Once mum's that big presence behind him, just reassuring.

357
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:57,320
 And of course that's what he'd get from his mother.

358
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:06,320
 One of the things that I love about elephants, and you can see it happening right here in front of you,

359
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:09,320
 is the empathy that they have for one another.

360
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:11,320
 These two elephants aren't related.

361
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:16,320
 It's not a mother and girl, but you'd never know it, because they really do seem to care.

362
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:22,320
 And actually, I think it's essential to a rock for little elephant to have that kind of nurturing right now.

363
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:27,320
 He needs it, and Nacilok knows it, and she's prepared to give it to him.

364
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,320
 That's just the most wonderful thing.

365
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:34,320
 So, life's looking great for a rock.

366
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:40,320
 And the keepers tell me that the other two little lilies who came up with him have also settled in really well.

367
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:41,320
 But what about Wendy?

368
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:46,320
 Well, it looks as if things have really turned around for her too.

369
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:49,320
 I mean, just look at Wendy.

370
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:53,320
 Now, when we brought those three little orphans from Nairobi up here to a thumber,

371
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:56,320
 we thought that Wendy perhaps would adopt the role of the matriarch.

372
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,320
 She would be like a mother to them.

373
00:20:58,320 --> 00:21:01,320
 Well, it didn't happen, but look at her now.

374
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:07,320
 She's beginning to actually move away from that dependence on people and become an elephant,

375
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:11,320
 to be part of the herd, just to have fun, just to enjoy herself.

376
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:16,320
 Nacilok says if she's growing up a little bit, but very much now connected with being an elephant,

377
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:19,320
 and that's just what we wanted.

378
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,320
 So, what could have prompted Wendy's change of heart?

379
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:27,320
 Maybe, with three new babies in the herd occupying the keepers' attention,

380
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:32,320
 she decided it was time to look to the other elephants for companionship again.

381
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:40,320
 We'll never know the answer, but what I can definitely say is that she's back to being her old happy self again.

382
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:47,320
 Up in Nairobi, it's a big day for Underlolo.

383
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:53,320
 After weeks of treatment, it's time to see if there's been any improvement in his eyesight.

384
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:58,320
 The result could decide whether he has any chance of a life back in the wild.

385
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:03,320
 Angela Scheldrick Daffney's daughter has brought the vet to see him.

386
00:22:03,320 --> 00:22:11,320
 Angela, there's no question the opacity is much reduced.

387
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,320
 There's no question of that.

388
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:15,320
 And he is a bit visual.

389
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:22,320
 He can see me, he could see, he could distinguish myself a little bit, and that's why he was looking at me.

390
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:26,320
 But also, all these other senses have compensated.

391
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:27,320
 Yeah.

392
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,320
 That's the bird eye, Sanjay.

393
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,320
 Yeah.

394
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:32,320
 See the wind just just on there.

395
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:33,320
 I can see the thunder.

396
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:35,320
 I can see the thunder. I can see it.

397
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:37,320
 This is really good.

398
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:39,320
 I'm not surprised you can see so well.

399
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,320
 So you think there's definitely some vision?

400
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:43,320
 Yeah, definitely.

401
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,320
 Definitely.

402
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:46,320
 Yeah.

403
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,320
 Light and dark and shape.

404
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:48,320
 Yeah.

405
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,320
 Yeah.

406
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:50,320
 Exactly.

407
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,320
 You're going to be all right.

408
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,320
 Isn't that amazing?

409
00:22:56,320 --> 00:23:02,320
 It's fantastic news for everyone, especially under low-low.

410
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:14,320
 It's nightfall in Ithumba and the elephants have returned to the stock aid.

411
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:19,320
 They sleep behind electric fences to keep them in and predators out.

412
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:27,320
 Using specialized equipment, I'm going to get a unique insight into what Wendy and Iraq do once the lights go out.

413
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:31,320
 It's such a privilege to come up to the stock aid at night.

414
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,320
 I mean, it's a different world.

415
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:38,320
 Because after all, remember the night, particularly for the little ones, must be really scary.

416
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:42,320
 Little Iraq recently having moved here from Nairobi.

417
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:48,320
 I mean, if it wasn't for Nastalok, this big elephant that's acting as mum to them, this would be a really tough time for them.

418
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:59,320
 Now, next door to Nastalok and Iraq and these elephants, we've got the youngsters, the adolescents.

419
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:01,320
 We've got Wendy and her charms.

420
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:04,320
 And, I mean, they are just like a naughty bunch of school kids.

421
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:09,320
 They've been sent to bed, the lights are out, and suddenly it's like, okay, is it safe?

422
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:10,320
 Can we just start mucking around?

423
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:12,320
 I mean, they're having such fun.

424
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:25,320
 You can see that Iraq is determined to stay as close as he can, just as he does during the daytime, to Nastalok, to his surrogate mum.

425
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:32,320
 And, I mean, it must be so comforting for him because, remember, this little elephant, he lost his herd.

426
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:38,320
 He lost his mum when he was 18 months old, so he has a real memory of the wild herd.

427
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:42,320
 So this must be just heaven for that little elephant.

428
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:48,320
 Next door, Wendy's thoroughly enjoying her newfound friendships.

429
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:52,320
 She's not allowing her sleepover charms to get any rest at all.

430
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:57,320
 You can see Nastalok's eyes now just beginning to droop.

431
00:24:57,320 --> 00:25:02,320
 She's obviously very tired, and the reason I'm sure it is, is because she's got new responsibilities.

432
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:08,320
 She's got a little elephant, little or rock to look after, and it's obviously taking it out of her.

433
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:15,320
 There she goes. Nastalok's finally given in. She's just toppling over, just going down on her side.

434
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:19,320
 Oh, that must feel so good.

435
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:29,320
 You can see that Iraq, I mean, it's just like during the daytime.

436
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:36,320
 He wants to be as close as he possibly can to Nastalok, so he's curled up there, and he's right just between her legs.

437
00:25:36,320 --> 00:25:40,320
 It's just like a cradle for him. He must feel so contented doing that.

438
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:49,320
 That's lovely. The way Wendy and the others now, they finally had enough.

439
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:52,320
 The party's over, and they're going to get some sleep.

440
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:59,320
 This really proves to me that both Wendy and Iran have found their place in the family.

441
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,320
 They seem so content.

442
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:16,320
 Up in Nairobi, morning brings unexpected and totally devastating news.

443
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:25,320
 Little Andalolo has died very suddenly, and the keepers are in shock.

444
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:55,320
 He was fine. I started coming back, putting on weight, lively, feeding well.

445
00:26:55,320 --> 00:27:01,320
 And then he just suddenly went off his food in the morning and was dead an hour later.

446
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:06,320
 So, we were all devastated, of course.

447
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:13,320
 Tragedy was that we really thought he had a chance, and he did say one to live.

448
00:27:13,320 --> 00:27:21,320
 We all loved him to bits, but it was not to be.

449
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:29,320
 Edwin has seen his share of tragedies here, but this death has hit him very hard.

450
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:33,320
 I feel very sad and very shocked about it.

451
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:36,320
 Of course, I loved that baby elephant.

452
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:47,320
 The trusted absolutely everything they could to save this little calf.

453
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:52,320
 Across their three centres, they currently care for over 50 orphaned elephants,

454
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:56,320
 but almost the same number have been rescued and not made it.

455
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:59,320
 And these are tough statistics for the team to live with.

456
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:05,320
 Every elephant is precious, but for Daphne and the whole team in Nairobi,

457
00:28:05,320 --> 00:28:08,320
 this particular little elephant will never be forgotten.

458
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:14,320
 And the fight to save Kenya's wild orphans will go on.

459
00:28:14,320 --> 00:28:22,320
 Next time on Elephant Diaries, we've just heard from Daphne that another orphan has been brought into the stockade up a boy,

460
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:26,320
 and I'm just hoping that it's in a lot better condition than it will and Delolo was.

461
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:28,320
 Let's go and check him out.

462
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:37,320
 To discover more about elephants and the people who work with them,

463
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:41,320
 visit bbc.co.uk/nature.

464
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:46,320
 And if you miss super giant animals with Steve Bakshor,

465
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:50,320
 last night on BBC One, take a look now on BBC iPlayer.

